## Why This Is Asked

Addresses real-world needs for analytics while protecting sensitive SAP data. Evaluates understanding of data masking, per-tenant access control, and end-to-end data lineage.

## Key Concepts

- SAP data export pipelines to data lakes
- Field-level masking for PII/financial data
- Deterministic masking to preserve join feasibility
- IAM SCPs and per-tenant roles for isolation
- Data lineage via Glue Data Catalog
- KMS encryption at rest; minimal IaC for keys/roles

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: deterministic mask preserving format
function maskForColumn(val){ 
  if (val===null) return null;
  const s = String(val);
  const masked = s.replace(/[0-9]/g,'0');
  return masked.length>0 ? masked : val;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotence and integrity after multiple masking runs?
- What strategies ensure masking policies stay in sync with SAP authorization changes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to orchestrate low-downtime upgrades in SAP on AWS with native services, focusing on reliability, rollback, and measurable validation.

## Key Concepts
- Blue/Green deployments for SAP on EC2
- Route 53 weighted routing and health checks
- SSM automation for kernel patching
- CloudFormation for repeatable environments
- Validation: SAP status, HANA health, ABAP batch

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: update Route 53 weighted record to switch traffic
const { Route53Client, ChangeResourceRecordSetsCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-route-53');
const client = new Route53Client({ region: 'us-east-1' });
async function switchTraffic(hostedZoneId, recordName, weight) {
  const params = {
    HostedZoneId: hostedZoneId,
    ChangeBatch: {
      Changes: [
        {
          Action: 'UPSERT',
          ResourceRecordSet: {
            Name: recordName,
            Type: 'A',
            SetIdentifier: weight > 50 ? 'Green' : 'Blue',
            Weight: weight,
            TTL: 60
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  };
  return client.send(new ChangeResourceRecordSetsCommand(params));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback safety if the Green stack patch causes SAP instability?
- What metrics would you capture to decide promotion vs rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical use of AWS SSM Patch Manager, IAM roles, and CloudWatch in SAP ops.

## Key Concepts
- Systems Manager Patch Manager
- IAM roles and trust policies
- Maintenance windows
- CloudWatch alarms and SNS

## Code Example
```javascript
const cf = {
  Resources: {
    SAPPatchRole: {
      Type: 'AWS::IAM::Role',
      Properties: {
        AssumeRolePolicyDocument: {
          Version: '2012-10-17',
          Statement: [ { Effect: 'Allow', Principal: { Service: 'ec2.amazonaws.com' }, Action: 'sts:AssumeRole' } ]
        },
        ManagedPolicyArns: [ 'arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore' ],
        Policies: [ { PolicyName: 'SAPPatchArtifactAccess', PolicyDocument: { Version: '2012-10-17', Statement: [ { Effect: 'Allow', Action: [ 's3:GetObject','s3:PutObject','s3:ListBucket' ], Resource: [ 'arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-bucket', 'arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-bucket/*' ] } ] } } ]
      }
    },
    SAPPatchAssociation: { Type: 'AWS::SSM::Association', Properties: { Name: 'AWS-RunPatchBaseline', InstanceId: { Ref: 'SAPInstance' }, ScheduleExpression: 'rate(1 day)' } }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test patch-failure alarms in a non-production environment?
- What additional controls would you add to prevent patch drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, auditable cross-account access that bridges SAP authorizations with AWS IAM, while using JIT and MFA in a multi-region, multi-account setup. Tests integration points across IAM, SCPs, SSO, auditing, and basic IaC.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account trust and least privilege
- SCPs and IAM role mappings to SAP authorizations
- Just‑In‑Time elevation with AWS SSO and MFA
- Auditing: CloudTrail, Config, Central logging
- Minimal IaC for trust role and VPC endpoint service

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Terraform-like snippet for cross-account trust role (pseudo)
provider "aws" { alias = "shared" }
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator_trust" {
  name = "sap-operator-cross-account"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Principal = { AWS = ["arn:aws:iam::111111111111:root"] },
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
        Condition = { StringEquals = { "sts:ExternalId" = "sap-access" } }
      }
    ]
  })
}

// Per‑BU session policy (inline for example)
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "sap-operator-permission"
  role = aws_iam_role.sap_operator_trust.name
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["ec2:Describe*"], Resource = "*" },
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["sap:*"], Resource = "*" }
    ]
  })
}

// VPC Endpoint Service placeholder
resource "aws_vpc_endpoint_service" "sap_endpoints" {
  acceptance_required = true
  network_load_balancer_arns = [aws_lb.sap_nlb.arn]
}
```

